;;; (6) A diagonal right factor: every order-s subdeterminant of X D is divisible
;;;     by the product of the first s diagonal entries of D (no Cauchy-Binet: the
;;;     submatrix of X D on (p, q) is the submatrix of X times the diagonal submatrix
;;;     of D on (q, q)).  Used by the uniqueness of the principal sequence (3.48).
